  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Response and Prevention of Disease Outbreak in Shabwah , Reserve Allocation 8</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM is scaling up essential Health and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) services in underserved areas in Yemen to support the urgent prevention and response to water-related and communicable disease outbreaks in the Radum and Habban districts in Shabwah. IOM is ensuring direct assistance in acute watery diarrhoea (AWD)/Cholera hotspots for an estimated 26,340 affected internally displaced persons (IDPs) and host communities, with specific modalities to reach migrants who are one of the most vulnerable groups in Yemen and disproportionally suffer from lack of access to basic services.</narrative>
  </description>
